---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CONTACT } from "../consts";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What dynshift.com collects: nothing of its own. What Google's advertising does collect here, what choices you have, and where each product's own policy lives."
>
  <section class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="muted small">Last updated 23 September 2026.</p>

    <h2>What DynShift collects</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Nothing.</strong> This site has no accounts, no forms, no
      newsletter and no analytics of any kind. DynShift does not set a cookie
      here, does not profile you, and does not sell or share anything about
      you, because it has nothing to sell or share.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site is static and hosted on GitHub Pages. As with any web host,
      GitHub's servers see the request for each page, including your IP
      address, and handle it under
      <a
        href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
        rel="noopener">GitHub's privacy statement</a
      >. DynShift does not receive or keep those logs.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      This site is funded by advertising, and that is the honest reason it is
      here: the tools DynShift publishes are free, and advertising pays for the
      time that goes into them.
    </p>
    <p>
      The advertising is supplied by <strong>Google AdSense</strong>. Every page
      loads Google's advertising script; a few long-form pages carry a single
      advertisement, labelled <em>Advertisement</em> and separated from the text
      by a rule above and below it. There are none on the home page, none on
      this page, none in the navigation or the footer, and none placed where a
      mistimed tap would hit one instead of a link.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google, as the provider, may set cookies or read similar identifiers in
      your browser to serve and measure those advertisements, and in some
      regions to personalise them. What Google does with that data is described
      in
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener"
        >how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a
      > and in
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener"
        >Google's advertising policies</a
      >. DynShift sees none of it: what reaches the studio is a count of
      earnings, never a visitor.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>In the EEA, the UK and Switzerland</strong>, Google's consent
        message appears on your first visit and asks before anything is used to
        personalise advertising. Your answer is recorded and respected. To
        change it afterwards, use <strong>Privacy settings</strong> in the
        footer of any page; that control appears only where the message
        applies.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Anywhere</strong>, you can turn off personalised advertising for
        your Google account at
        <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noopener">My Ad Center</a>,
        and block or delete cookies in your browser's settings. Blocking them
        does not break this site: it is static pages and text.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>If you use an ad blocker</strong>, nothing here will argue with
        it. There is no wall, no nag, and no counting of who blocks what.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Product sites</h2>
    <p>
      Each DynShift product lives on its own site with its own policy, which is
      the one that applies there. The products themselves are not this site:
      PhonePad, for one, collects nothing at all and talks to no server.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://phonepad.dynshift.com/privacy/">PhonePad</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://layr.dynshift.com/" rel="noopener">Layr</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy, or about anything held about you:
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  section {
    padding-block: clamp(24px, 5vw, 56px);
  }
</style>
